00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:33.000
Now, that's not to say that the communal ones aren't incredibly important because we need social support. We need all kinds of things to get through grief. And that's the bad news, that losing those really does have an impact. The good news is we can have a little bit of flexibility in creating our own, and those can help too. One of the rituals that you've studied is the simple handshake. That's something else that we can't engage in right now. Even Dr. Anthony Fauci has suggested maybe facetiously that we may never shake hands again. Do you think that's the case?
现在，这并不是说公共的并不极其重要，因为我们需要社会支持。我们需要各种各样的事情来度过悲伤。这就是坏消息，失去那些确实会产生影响。好消息是我们在创造自己的方面可以有一点灵活性，那些也能有所帮助。你研究过的仪式之一是简单的握手。那是我们现在无法参与的另一件事。甚至安东尼·福奇博士也半开玩笑地建议我们可能再也不会握手了。你认为会这样吗？

