good. And of course, we know that because rituals taken too far can become a symptom of obsessive compulsive disorder, which we know isn't good. So we know that it's not just that more rituals is better. And I would never want anyone to think that what I'm saying is more rituals is better. They have to be used when it's appropriate. But another way that they're not good for us as well is you're absolutely right. They bond us together. But in the bonding us together, they can drive us apart from other people. When I talk about this, I do have people stand up and perform a ritual in groups, and I made it up. And I just, and I say, here's something I made up. Can we all do it together? And it's things like clapping and stomping your hands and things like that. And all I say to
好的。当然，我们知道这一点，因为走得太远的仪式会成为强迫症的症状，我们知道这不好。所以我们知道，并不是仪式越多越好。我绝不希望任何人认为我的意思是仪式越多越好。它们必须在适当的时候使用。但它们对我们不好的另一个方面是，你说得绝对没错。它们把我们绑在一起。但在把我们绑在一起的过程中，它们会把我们从其他人身边推开。当我谈到这一点时，我确实让人们站起来，以小组为单位表演一个仪式，这是我编造的。我只是，我说，这是我编造的。我们能一起做吗？这些事情包括拍手、跺脚等等。我所说的只是

