the group is, go ahead. And what happens is people start the ritual and they very quickly get in sync so that everyone starts clapping at the same time and then stomping at the same time. And they really like it. They feel good about each other. They're looking around smile. It's like, this is our ritual. It's great. But you also see that if someone, quote, unquote, messes up, meaning that I clap instead of stomp at the wrong time, people get very angry at the person. So they look at them, you know, what's wrong with you? And when I asked them at the end, what did you think about those people? They say, well, you know, he was doing it wrong. Now, remember, I told them I just made up this ritual that they've never done before. There's no wrong. There's no wrong. There's no right. I just made it up. I told them I just made it up. And yet immediately, that quickly we can say, this is the good way, we do it this way, and if you do it the other way, I don't like you. And we do see that in two separate projects. So with Tammy Kim, we showed that rituals can bond us together. And with Nick Thompson, we showed actually that rituals can drive us apart in exactly this way. So let's talk for a minute about rituals and clothing.
对这个小组，开始吧。发生的事情是，人们开始这个仪式，他们很快就合拍了，以至于每个人都同时开始拍手，然后同时跺脚。他们真的很喜欢它。他们对彼此感觉很好。他们环顾四周，微笑着。就像，这是我们的仪式，太棒了。但你也会看到，如果有人，也就是所谓的，搞砸了，意思是说我在错误的时间拍手而不是跺脚，人们会对这个人非常生气。所以他们看着他们，你知道，你怎么了？当我在最后问他们，你们怎么看那些人时？他们说，嗯，你知道，他做错了。现在，请记住，我告诉过他们，我只是编造了这个他们从未做过的新仪式。没有错的。没有错的。没有对的。我只是编造的。我告诉过他们我只是编造的。然而，很快，我们可以说，这是好方法，我们这样做，如果你用另一种方法，我不喜欢你。我们在两个独立的项目中确实看到了这一点。因此，通过与塔米·金（Tammy Kim）合作，我们证明了仪式可以把我们凝聚在一起。通过与尼克·汤普森（Nick Thompson）合作，我们实际上证明了仪式可以以这种确切的方式将我们推开。所以我们花一分钟来谈谈仪式与服装。

