A lot of us have spent the last couple, almost two months in sweatpants or pajamas most of the day. And a popular meme on social media asks, when was the last time you wore pants? with buttons. So I think we know that clothing has meaning in pretty much every culture. What are some of the actual rituals surrounding clothing and how do they affect us psychologically? One of the very first things we did when we started studying rituals was we asked research assistants to find every grieving ritual that any human group had ever enacted in human history. So that was their task and we set them loose. And pretty much every recorded culture has a grieving ritual. It's something that often has communal elements. And we know this. Whatever culture you're in, you know exactly the one in your
